WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- Hi.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.499
- Hi.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.460
- You have a talk show.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.749
- I know,

00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:08.582
(laughs)

00:00:08.582 --> 00:00:10.580
How did you end up becoming one of like

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.040
the great entrepreneurs of life

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.790
and I ended up on a talk show?

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.750
Like it's been almost 22 years.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.190
I think it has been 22 years

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.010
since Never Been Kissed.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.880
- Yeah, isn't that a trip?

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.033
I had my 17th birthday on the set.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.410
- Aaw!

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.890
I mean we...
- I've Never Been Kissed.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:33.370
- Just had the best time making that film.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.310
- Yeah and everyone,

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.900
I mean you popped so many actors as well.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.840
I mean It felt like camp,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:39.950
but you also,

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.700
I mean you really took so many people

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.610
under your wing

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.810
and,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.643
guided them

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:47.980
and a lot of us were
just really starting out

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.340
and you set the stage,

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.340
I would say for us

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.970
and gave us a platform to be successful.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.629
So, thank you.

00:00:56.629 --> 00:00:57.462
(audience claps)

00:00:57.462 --> 00:01:00.570
- I mean, if I had anything to do with

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:04.200
some of your origin story
which I'm so proud to.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.720
Holy cow! did you,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.550
just come out of the gate swinging?

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:10.870
I mean,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.780
it's just astonishing to me

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.220
that you were the one and so amazing.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.960
Your light bulb went off

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:22.170
and you became an
extraordinary business woman,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.010
but at the same time provided

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:26.283
a whole different avenue for moms.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:27.963
- Yeah you know,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.760
I guess it just came out of,

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.480
I went lobbied on Capitol
Hill for chemical reform

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.850
because I looked at this data around

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.100
the rise in illnesses,

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.800
basically coinciding

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.520
with the rise of the
industrialization of chemicals

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.210
that have been brought
into the marketplace

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.500
and put into

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.740
every single,

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.573
category

00:01:50.573 --> 00:01:53.330
from detergents to baby products,

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.360
to makeup.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.380
And it's making people sick

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.300
at like astronomical numbers.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.133
And then when you look at

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.070
the Black and Brown communities

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.560
and I'm obviously part of that community.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.400
I really felt like it was
a social justice issue.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.650
And so I wanted to solve this

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.670
social justice issue

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.170
and also create a for-profit business

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.540
to sustain that initiative.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.820
And then being able to give back

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.950
to families who were born
in unfortunate circumstances

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.203
and that's where a percentage of sales,

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.260
products,

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.550
and time

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.730
we donate since day one

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.700
at The Honest Company.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.310
Our biggest partner has been BABY2BABY.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.570
- And if you go to our website,

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.060
you'll be able to access all information

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.620
as well as a way to get
involved with BABY2BABY,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.710
which is a company I've
been involved with now

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:48.670
for eight or nine years.

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.770
- You've been part of it up close

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.760
and your involvement in it

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.250
has actually allowed us

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.310
from being,

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.680
a nonprofit

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.990
that really was just
affecting one community

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.180
in Los Angeles and being
able to expand nationally.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.100
Especially now that a
lot of kids due to Covid,

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.953
aren't able to go to,

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.100
you know pre-school

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.800
or to school.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.220
They're not able to get
a lot of those essentials

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.330
but we have been able to

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.930
navigate through a lot
of those challenges,

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.430
and even at Honest,

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.770
we were able to develop

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.500
a solution with disinfecting sprays.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.940
A disinfecting spray,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.280
a wipe that's made from over 65% alcohol,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.580
our hand sanitizer spray,

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.530
and masks for children and for adults.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:42.170
And so we're also donating
to families in need with

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.231
the masks and sanitizers and stuff.

00:03:44.231 --> 00:03:45.064
(audience clapping)

00:03:45.064 --> 00:03:45.897
- Okay, straight talk.

00:03:45.897 --> 00:03:47.350
How are you doing it?

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.900
You know we as women like

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.520
don't wanna ever not say

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:52.600
you can't have it all

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.810
you can't do it all.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.010
But I just spent my weekend you know

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.680
I'm in like a whole self-improvement surge

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.410
for like how I talk to
myself in my own head.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.310
And in my inner dialogue

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.880
was not very nice this weekend.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.090
It was you know

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:08.923
(laughs)

00:04:08.923 --> 00:04:11.360
How is a mom with your kids and your job

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.193
and everything.

00:04:12.193 --> 00:04:13.490
How's your inner voice?

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:14.330
How is it?

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.580
(chuckles)

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:18.323
- Real talk.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.580
I told everyone in the family

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.032
that I need a break from them.

00:04:23.032 --> 00:04:24.030
(laughs)

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.400
So Kelly and I are actually gonna go away

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.880
for a week.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:29.780
And I don't really know

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.330
what we're getting ourselves into.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.840
I just know

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.150
that I can't be around my family anymore.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.090
Cause I literally (chuckles)

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:38.923
I've had it.

00:04:38.923 --> 00:04:40.350
I've had enough.

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.420
I just like, it's like,

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.020
and they all come down on me.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:43.930
I'm like (chuckles)

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.407
you guys every time they ask me like,

00:04:45.407 --> 00:04:46.700
"Mom, can I download this app?"

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:47.793
Or "Mom, can I get on the FaceTime mom?"

00:04:47.793 --> 00:04:48.780
"Mom can I..."

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.970
and "Mom I'm hungry"

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.517
and "Is this outfit okay?"

00:04:52.517 --> 00:04:53.350
"Can you help me?"

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.420
I'm like you're on a Zoom call.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.730
Like don't talk to me.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.570
I'm like talk to your dad

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:00.580
and then I just start nagging.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.700
And then I'm just nagging

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.020
and I'm that person.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:05.853
And they're like,

00:05:05.853 --> 00:05:07.800
"Mom, your tone, you're so mean,"

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:08.787
you know and Cash is like,

00:05:08.787 --> 00:05:10.320
"Gosh! I guess, you know

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.490
I guess I'm just gonna
go back into my man room'

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:13.323
and I'm like,

00:05:13.323 --> 00:05:14.720
what else is new.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.150
(laughs loudly)

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.720
Disappearing, for me to
deal with every thing.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.140
So, yes, it's been fun,

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.550
it's been really fun.
(laughs loudly)

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:23.630
Now imagine,

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.540
I mean you have my nine year old

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.500
she doesn't wanna go to bed,

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.270
it's a fight every night.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:31.270
- It is, I'm in hell right now
- Oh my.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:32.370
- Because I slept.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:34.200
- I'm like, are we renew it,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.033
like what?

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:37.350
You know, you need to go to bed kid.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:38.570
This isn't a thing.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.560
We shouldn't talk about this.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.667
And so I just said and she goes,

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.010
"Well you make dinner so late

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.060
every time you make dinner."

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:45.963
And am just like,
(laughs loudly)

00:05:45.963 --> 00:05:47.730
here's the thing,

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.780
here's the thing

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.110
I'm gonna make dinner late.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.210
You're gonna eat late

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.970
and then you're gonna get your butt to bed

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:54.190
right after that

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:55.690
and that's just the way it's gonna be.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:56.830
That's just the way it's gonna be.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:57.760
I don't know what to say

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:58.730
I'm not perfect

00:05:58.730 --> 00:05:59.762
you're gonna eat dinner late.

00:05:59.762 --> 00:06:00.595
(audience claps)

00:06:00.595 --> 00:06:01.428
- Oh my God!

00:06:01.428 --> 00:06:04.050
I already have loved you for 22 years.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.280
And I just fall more and more in love

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.750
for so many reasons

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.590
but I just thank you

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.760
because I feel so much less alone.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:12.593
(laughs)

00:06:12.593 --> 00:06:15.760
(bright upbeat music)

